  "notepad": {
    "activeNoteIndex": 0,
    "notes": [
      {
        "name": "How to read this sheet",
        "content": "QA-01 — every component type at its authored defaults.\n\nGenerated by tools/scripts/qa/make-qa-panels.mjs. Do not hand-edit: regenerate instead, or your\nchanges vanish the next time a component is added.\n\nHow to read it\n  Each control sits under a caption naming its type. Everything here is at the default a user\n  gets when they drag the component onto a blank canvas — nothing is configured.\n\nWhat a failure looks like\n  - a blank cell                      the renderer threw, or draws nothing at defaults\n  - a control the size of its caption  the type's defaultOverrides lost its Transform\n  - text reading \"Label\" or \"Button\"   correct: that IS the authored default\n  - a cell that overlaps its neighbour the component ignores its Transform width/height\n\nWhat this sheet does NOT prove\n  Nothing here is interactive, bound, or scripted. A component can render perfectly at defaults\n  and still be broken the moment it is dragged, bound to a device, or driven from a script.\n  That is QA-03 through QA-06."
      }
    ]
  },
